mapping "V9140.1" source="V9140" target="215414001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V9140 SNOMED CT 215414001 = Swedish national extension of WHO ICD-10 V91.4 (Accident to
        watercraft causing other injury, sailboat) qualified with activity = sport/exercise. Target
        SNOMED CT 438301 (concept_code 215414001, Water transport accident) is the standard concept the WHO
        base V91.4 code maps to via the Athena ICD10→SNOMED CT crosswalk (45604819 Maps to 438301). The
        sailboat specificity and the activity qualifier (sport) have no separate SNOMED CT standard target;
        the target fully subsumes the water-transport-accident axis but is broader on both
        watercraft-type and activity dimensions. Moderate tier: verified crosswalk for the WHO base
        code, but the Swedish extension adds two specificity layers (vessel subtype + activity) lost in
        mapping, not independently re-verified.
        """
}
